.TH EUCLID-CLI-EMM 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-emm \- inspect the Euclid module manager's live module pool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-loglevel\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
.B emm
.I action
[\fIaction-options\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B emm
module talks directly to the Euclid gateway itself, rather than to a
separate module process the way
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1)
and
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1)
do - the gateway
.RI ( euclid-mgr )
answers
.B emm
requests locally, reading straight from the module repository (Mongo or
in-memory, per
.IR euclid.database.backend ).
.PP
Every
.B emm
command requires the caller to be authenticated as an administrator; see
.B AUTHENTICATION
below.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B list-modules
Lists every module known to the manager, one entry per module name, each
with its live pool of instances (pid, state, socket, restart count).
See
.BR euclid-cli-emm-list-modules (1).
.TP
.B export
Exports one or more modules' own MongoDB collections to a local JSON
file. See
.BR euclid-cli-emm-export (1).
.TP
.B import
Imports a JSON file written by
.B export
back into MongoDB. See
.BR euclid-cli-emm-import (1).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These options are given to
.B euclid-cli
itself, before the
.I emm
module name.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-endpoint " " \fIURL\fR
Euclid gateway endpoint to talk to, e.g. \fIhttps://localhost:5566\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-ca\-cert " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to a PEM CA certificate to trust in addition to the system trust
store, e.g. for self-signed development certificates.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to a JSON configuration file (currently used by
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1)
only). Defaults to
.IR /usr/local/euclid/etc/euclid.json ;
silently ignored if the file doesn't exist.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-signature " " \fISCHEME\fR
Signature scheme used for signed service calls: \fIsigv4\fR (the
default) or \fIrfc9421\fR for RFC 9421 HTTP Message Signatures. Both
prove the request with the same access key; RFC 9421 puts the
signature in \fISignature\fR/\fISignature\-Input\fR headers and binds
the body through \fIContent\-Digest\fR (RFC 9530) instead of using
AWS's Authorization header. Overrides
.I euclid.cli.signature
from the configuration file. Ignored for
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1)
commands, which authenticate with the session's bearer token.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-loglevel " " \fILEVEL\fR
Log level: one of \fItrace\fR, \fIdebug\fR, \fIinfo\fR, \fIwarning\fR,
\fIerror\fR, \fIfatal\fR. Defaults to \fIinfo\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print top-level usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the euclid-cli version and exit.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
.B emm
commands are authenticated using the session created by
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
loaded from
.IR $HOME/.euclid/credentials .
Like
.BR esm (1)
and
.BR eqs (1)
requests, they are signed with SigV4 using the stored access key ID and
secret if present, falling back to the bearer token otherwise.
.PP
Every
.B emm
action additionally requires the logged-in user to be an administrator.
The CLI checks the
.I isAdmin
flag stored in
.I $HOME/.euclid/credentials
(recorded there on login) before sending the request, so a non-admin
session fails immediately with a clear local error instead of a round
trip. This is a convenience only, not the security boundary: the gateway
independently re-checks the caller's administrator status on every
request regardless of what the client sends, and rejects the request
with
.I "HTTP 403"
if it isn't satisfied.
.PP
If your stored session predates this check (i.e. you logged in before
.I isAdmin
was recorded), run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again to refresh it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The action completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The stored session is missing or not an administrator's, the request
could not be sent, or the server rejected it. Details are printed to
standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.euclid/credentials
JSON file holding the current session's bearer token, SigV4 access key
and
.I isAdmin
flag, created by
.B euclid-cli eam login
and read by every
.B emm
action.
.SH EXAMPLES
List every module the manager knows about:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 emm list-modules
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export EQS's queues (and, with \fB\-\-full\fR, its messages too) to a
JSON file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 emm export --module eqs

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 emm export \e
    --module eqs --full --file eqs-backup.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Round-trip that file back in:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 emm import --file eqs-backup.json
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm-list-modules (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm-export (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm-import (1)
